{"nodes": [{"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "label": "Prefix Sum Array", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model / The Invariant", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Precompute once, query Theta(1). n+1 entries with prefix[0]=0 and half-open ranges is not a convention but what makes prefix[r]-prefix[l] work for every l<=r without a special case \u2014 and it matches Rust's &a[l..r] slice convention as a continual consistency check."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_difference_array", "label": "Difference Array", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model / Mechanics", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The exact dual of prefix sums \u2014 prefix-sum and difference are discrete integration and differentiation. Range updates become two point updates: Theta(n+u) where naive is Theta(n*u). The 'invert it' lens."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_invertibility_requirement", "label": "Invertibility Requirement", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "The Invariant / Pitfalls", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "prefix[r]-prefix[l] works because addition has an inverse. Min and max do not: from min(0..r)=3 and min(0..l)=3 you cannot determine min(l..r). Sums, XOR (self-inverse), counts, and non-zero products work; min/max/gcd need a sparse table or segment tree."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_2d_prefix_sums", "label": "2-D Prefix Sums (Inclusion-Exclusion)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "2-D prefix sums", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The -p[i-1][j-1] in the build and the +p[r1][c1] in the query are the same inclusion-exclusion correction for the doubly-counted corner. Foundation of integral images and Viola-Jones face detection."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_plus_hashmap", "label": "Prefix Sums + HashMap (Subarray Sum with Negatives)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Prefix sums + hash map", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "sum(l..r)==k iff prefix[l]==prefix[r]-k, so counting subarrays becomes counting earlier prefix values in Theta(1). Theta(n) and sign-agnostic \u2014 the fix for the sliding-window limitation \u2014 and generalizes to divisibility (key on running % k) and balance problems."}, {"id": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_overflow_widening", "label": "Widen the Prefix Array Type", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The prefix array's magnitude grows with n, not with the element range \u2014 it is a fundamentally larger quantity built from the same values. Always i64/u64 prefix over i32 data."}], "edges": [{"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_difference_array", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Mental Model \u2014 exact duals", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_invertibility_requirement", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "The Invariant", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_2d_prefix_sums", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "2-D prefix sums", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_plus_hashmap", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Prefix sums + hash map", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_overflow_widening", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfalls in Depth", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_invertibility_requirement", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_fenwick_tree", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "The Invariant \u2014 'same limitation as the Fenwick tree'", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_invertibility_requirement", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_sparse_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfall: Using prefix sums for min or max", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_sum_array", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_range_query_structures_learning_does_the_data_change", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Pitfall: Rebuilding prefix sums after every update \u2014 links Stage 4", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "data_structures_and_algorithms_prefix_sums_and_difference_arrays_learning_prefix_plus_hashmap", "target": "data_structures_and_algorithms_monotonic_stack_and_queue_learning_monotonic_deque", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.75, "source_file": "data-structures-and-algorithms/prefix-sums-and-difference-arrays/learning.md", "source_location": "Both are the Theta(n) repair for a sliding-window limitation \u2014 one for negative sums, one for min/max", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}